findings.description:
The design names handling for suite timeout, `SuiteRunError`, `CodeHostError` and resolver import failure. It does not say what happens when:
- the `gh` GraphQL call hangs (421 D12 declares timeouts for install, suite and probe only);
- `pytest --collect-only` hangs;
- the boundary resolver hangs or is killed;
- the trace run has no named runner or bound;
- a git command fails, for example when the parent is absent from a shallow clone and `parent..commit` cannot be diffed.

It also has no rule for unexpected exceptions. Each path needs a bound or handler, an observable signal and a test. Line 389 covers three paths only.
